# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, every file written on Windows carried CRLF, and `gofmt -l`
# reported 179 files as unformatted. 162 of those differed from gofmt's output
# by nothing but the line terminator -- which meant the 17 files with real
# formatting drift were indistinguishable from the noise, and the check was
# useless as a gate. See TODOS.md CI-003.
#
# eol=lf rather than eol=native on purpose: Go tooling writes LF, so a native
# checkout re-dirties every file gofmt touches.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.go text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.sum text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.env text eol=lf

# Binary, or content whose bytes are the point.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
